# Microsoft Entra ID Audit Logging and Zero Trust Validation

## Cedar Valley Health Zero Trust Identity Lab

## Objective

Audit logs were reviewed to verify administrative actions and maintain accountability within the Microsoft Entra ID environment.

---

# Audit Activities Reviewed

The following activities were validated:

- User creation
- Security group creation
- Group membership changes
- Administrative role assignments

---

# Zero Trust Final Review

## Identity

✅ Users created correctly  
✅ Departments assigned  
✅ Job titles added  

## Access Control

✅ Users placed into groups  
✅ Administrative roles limited  
✅ Least privilege applied  

## Monitoring

✅ Audit logs reviewed  
✅ Administrative changes verified  

---

# Zero Trust Principles Applied

## Verify Explicitly

Users were authenticated before receiving access.

## Least Privilege

Permissions were assigned based on job responsibilities.

## Assume Breach

Access was limited to reduce the impact of compromised accounts.

---

# Result

Audit logging confirmed visibility into identity changes and supported Cedar Valley Health's Zero Trust security model.
